WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.020
A decimal that stops is just a fraction whose bottom

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:06.590
number is ten, a hundred, a thousand, and so on.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.376
Nought point three seven five is three hundred

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:11.420
and seventy-five thousandths.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.640
And every power of ten is built from twos

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:15.790
and fives only.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.860
That one fact tells you which fractions make decimals

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.820
that stop, and which go on forever,

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.790
without doing any long division.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.080
Does three fortieths give a decimal that stops?

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:28.360
And what is it?

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:30.360
Pause and factorise forty.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:37.320
Forty is two times two times two times five.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.660
To make a power of ten, every two needs a five.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:43.020
There are three twos and one five,

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.060
so supply two more fives.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:47.520
Multiply top and bottom by twenty-five.

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:51.180
Three fortieths becomes seventy-five thousandths:

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:53.200
nought point nought seven five.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.880
Now try one sixth.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:57.420
Six is two times three.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:01.110
No amount of multiplying by twos and fives can turn that

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:03.220
three into part of a power of ten.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:07.770
So one sixth never stops: nought point one six

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:09.340
six six, forever.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.400
One warning: simplify first.

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:14.980
Six fifteenths has a three in the bottom,

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:15.840
but it cancels.

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.370
Six fifteenths is two fifths,

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:19.760
which is nought point four.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.820
Only the simplified fraction tells the truth.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.040
Decimals also hide divisibility.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:29.970
Nought point two five is a quarter, so multiplying by

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:31.500
four gives a whole number.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:35.130
A decimal with two places always becomes whole when

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:36.250
multiplied by one hundred,

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:38.700
and sometimes by something smaller.

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:40.780
Simplify the fraction.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.860
If the bottom is built only from twos and fives,

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:44.940
the decimal stops.

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:47.940
If any other prime remains, it repeats forever.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:50.740
Notebook challenge: which of these stop:

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:54.520
seven twentieths, five twelfths, nine seventy-fifths?
